    <!--
        Assignment 2.07. Worked example, and the answer to "why are my fields
        stacked vertically". Uncomment the record below when you reach 2.07.

        The nesting is what makes the columns. The outer group opens a column
        layout; each inner group becomes one column of labels and fields. A
        single group on its own gives you one column, everything stacked.

        A notebook holds the detail. Anything a user needs at a glance goes on
        the sheet above it; everything else earns a page.

        Three things worth reading closely as you uncomment it:

          header       the strip above the sheet. A statusbar shows the
                       workflow as a row of stages instead of a dropdown.
          oe_title     the large heading area at the top left of a sheet,
                       where the record's identity goes.
          currency_id  carries invisible="1". Monetary fields need their
                       currency on the form to render, but nobody needs to
                       see it.
    -->
    <!--
