    <!--
        TODO (assignment 2.08): two additions to the form above, once you have
        uncommented it in 2.07.

        1. tag_ids, on a line of its own directly above the first <group>.
           many2many_tags draws the links as coloured pills, and color_field
           says which field holds the palette index:

               <field name="tag_ids" widget="many2many_tags"
                      options="{'color_field': 'color'}"
                      placeholder="Tags..."/>

        2. a page titled "Compliance Checklist", after the Financials page,
           holding document_ids in an embedded editable list so paperwork can
           be added without leaving the loan:

               <page string="Compliance Checklist">
                   <field name="document_ids">
                       <list editable="bottom">
                           ... the columns you want ...
                       </list>
                   </field>
               </page>
    -->

    <!--
        TODO (assignment 2.07): the search view.

        id loan_application_view_search, on loan.application, wrapping a
        <search> element that holds three kinds of child.

        1. Searchable fields. These are what the box at the top matches when
           someone types:

               <field name="name"/>
               <field name="partner_id"/>

        2. Filters, one per shortcut. Each needs a name, a label, and a domain:

               <filter name="filter_draft" string="Draft"
                       domain="[('state', '=', 'draft')]"/>

           Add Archived, Draft and Approved. Archived filters on active rather
           than state, and the value is the Python False, not the text
           "false":

               domain="[('active', '=', False)]"

           Put a <separator/> between the Archived filter and the state ones.
           Filters in the same block are combined with OR, and a separator
           starts a new block, which is combined with AND. Without it,
           selecting Archived and Draft would show records that are either,
           rather than both.

        3. Group By options, which set a context instead of a domain. Wrap
           them in a plain group so they land in their own column of the
           dropdown:

               <group>
                   <filter name="group_by_state" string="Status"
                           context="{'group_by': 'state'}"/>
               </group>

           Add one for state and one for partner_id. Give every filter its own
           name: duplicates confuse Odoo about which one is active.

    -->

</odoo>
